specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/spec.md:1:# Feature Specification: Diedrico Dihedral Learning MVP
specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/spec.md:542:**Architecture**: All delete operations must go through CommandStack via DeleteElementsCommand. Direct World manipulation (e.g., `world.removePoint2D()`) is forbidden to ensure undo capability and dependency integrity.
specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/spec.md:544:**Note**: This is part of the broader architectural principle that ALL application state modifications (geometric, view, settings) should go through the CommandStack for consistent undo/redo behavior and state management.
specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/spec.md:660:- File list cached for 5 minutes (reduces API calls)
specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/spec.md:1267:  you should still have a viable MVP (Minimum Viable Product) that delivers value.
specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/spec.md:1538:- **FR-027**: The system MUST automatically persist project changes to Google Drive without requiring the user to explicitly save. Changes are debounced (e.g., 2 seconds after last change) to minimize API calls.
specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/spec.md:1575:- **FR-055**: The system MUST render the grid using the active projection plane's intrinsic coordinate system (u, v vectors), not arbitrary paper/canvas coordinates: the grid MUST be derived from the active plane's origin point (0, 0) and intrinsic u and v basis vectors, transformed through the plane's planeToPaper2D matrix to screen coordinates. Major grid lines MUST always be at multiples of powers of 10 (10^n where n is any integer, e.g., 0.1, 1, 10, 100, 1000), with the specific power chosen to maintain visual clarity at the current zoom level. Subdivisions between major lines MUST be exactly 2, 5, or 10, dividing each major interval into smaller cells. The subdivision count MUST be chosen to keep minor grid cells at or above a minimum pixel threshold (15 pixels), selecting the largest subdivision (10 > 5 > 2) that meets this requirement—this ensures maximum grid detail while preventing visual clutter. The algorithm MUST calculate minSpacing = minPixelsPerCell / zoom, then find the smallest value from the sequence (10^n/10, 10^n/5, 10^n/2) that is ≥ minSpacing, determining both the minor spacing and the corresponding major spacing (10^n). Major grid lines (at 10^n intervals) MUST be emphasized with darker color (#C0C0C0) compared to minor lines (#E0E0E0). Grid labels MUST display actual plane-local (u, v) coordinate values at major lines only, not transformed paper/canvas pixel coordinates. The plane's origin (0, 0) MUST be clearly visible when in viewport, marked by the intersection of u=0 and v=0 lines. The hinge line at v=0 MUST naturally align with horizontal grid lines on default planes. Each projection plane MUST show its own grid when active, derived from that plane's unique coordinate system and transformation matrices. The grid architecture MUST support future non-orthogonal planes where u, v vectors may be at arbitrary angles—transformation matrices already handle arbitrary orientations. [Phase 79 - Plane-Based Grid Coordinates]
specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/spec.md:1589:- The MVP includes at least two default projection planes (Horizontal and Vertical) and their hinge line.
specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/spec.md:1591:- The application is a web-based interactive tool; a backend service may be used for project persistence.
specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/spec.md:1592:- The MVP does not attempt to “fix” user mistakes; it surfaces infeasibility instead.
specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/spec.md:1632:- **FR-074**: The 3D view MUST render 3D lines (Line3DFromProjections, HingeLine, BrokenHingeLine, and other Line3D subclasses) with sufficient length to appear as infinite lines extending far beyond the typical viewport bounds, consistent with how 2D lines are rendered on projection planes. The rendering length MUST be at least 2000 units total (±1000 units from a point on the line), matching or exceeding the extension used for 2D lines in the 3D visualization. This ensures 3D lines provide proper spatial understanding and do not appear as small disconnected segments. [Phase 104 - Infinite 3D Line Rendering]
specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/spec.md:1650:- **FR-083**: When a new 2D element is created via an operation, the system MUST verify the element realizes to a feasible state immediately after creation. If immediately infeasible, the operation MUST log a warning but still allow creation (infeasibility may resolve when parent points are moved). All Element2D subclasses MUST implement an `isFeasible(world)` convenience method that calls `realize2D(world)` and returns the feasibility boolean. [Phase 114 - Feasibility Validation on Creation]
