specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/for-planing.md:81:  - **Problem**: Creation operations never check whether the newly created element is immediately infeasible. Infeasible elements are created silently and only show up as infeasible indicators during rendering. No `isFeasible()` convenience method exists on Element2D subclasses.
specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/for-planing.md:82:  - **Solution**: Add `isFeasible(world)` method to all Element2D subclasses. Add post-creation feasibility check in relevant operations. Log warnings for immediately-infeasible elements but allow creation (since moving parent points may fix it).
specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/for-planing.md:121:  - **Problem**: Segment3DFromProjections.realize3D() is a TODO stub returning placeholder coordinates. No compatibility validation at creation time. No process tree action recording.
specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/for-planing.md:146:  - **Solution**: Refactored constructors to receive parent objects (HingeLine/BrokenHingeLine) as primary parameters, making the geometric relationship explicit in the API. Fixed label extraction to correctly parse the line number from IDs like "projPlane28/line2d33" → "BHHL_{33}" (not "BHHL_{28}").
